  "authoringNote": "D2 regression (checkpoint #21). Both encounters are current (no supersedes metadata, C08), usable and final, and state different dates, so R04.encounters_disagree holds once with field encounter.date and names every final current usable encounter that states a date (both). Confidence, recency or document order never selects one. Each encounter pairs with the order: both dates precede 2026-09-01 within the six-month bound and identifiers match, so no pair condition holds. R04 is conflict (administrative reviewer, needs_human_review), parent set empty, and cites status, date and identifier of both encounters and the order (nine), so both conflicting dates are cited. R02 cites eight beneficiary facts, R06 ten clinical statements, R07 both false LCMP flags. R01, R03 and R05 are ordinary (eight, nine, four; the receipt follows the span end 2026-09-02T12:00Z). State needs_human_review. Full F14 reconciliation by arrival order is S4.",
